{"description":"Persist received and sent messages locally so history survives a restart, and enforce bounded retention on the coordinator side.\n\nLocal history is stored unencrypted, which walkie/adr:004-security-model names explicitly as an accepted MVP limitation. That limitation must be stated in the user documentation rather than left for a user to discover.","acceptanceCriteria":"1. History survives a client restart and is displayed in per-conversation order on reopen.\n2. History is queryable by conversation and by time range from the command line.\n3. Coordinator-side retention enforces both a time-to-live and a size cap; expiry is recorded in the logs.\n4. The store file is created with restrictive permissions.\n5. The documentation states plainly that local history is not encrypted at rest."}